{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104815","id":2427723684,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6QtB-k","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104815","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104815.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104815.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104815","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104815/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104815/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104815/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ec32dae1da20c375f8e1653da74ba88b3193e672","number":104815,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rename `_strlen_clipped` to `strnlen` (and use the system equivalent for `char *` inputs)","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I only now realized that the functionality is equivalent to [`strnlen`](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/strnlen.3.html).\r\nThe only difference is that `_strlen_clipped` takes an `int`, while `strnlen` takes `size_t`. We'll just let callers use `strlen` if they choose to accept negative arguments (as gdextension currently does).\r\n\r\n## Benchmark\r\nOf course I had to test this. `strnlen` is about 10x faster than `_strlen_clipped` we had implemented before:\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Code</summary>\r\n\r\nThis took a bit of tricker to prevent inlining (and bring in cache faults):\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n\tstatic constexpr size_t N = 10000;\r\n\tVector<char*> vector;\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000; ++i) {\r\n\t\tvector.append((char *)malloc(N));\r\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < N; ++j) {\r\n\t\t\tvector.ptr()[i][j] = 2;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tvector.ptr()[i][9000] = 0;\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < 10; ++j) {\r\n\t\t\tfor (uint64_t i = 0; i < vector.size(); i ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\ttest1(vector.ptr()[i], N);\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < 10; ++j) {\r\n\t\t\tfor (uint64_t i = 0; i < vector.size(); i ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\ttest2(vector.ptr()[i], N);\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd in a separate file:\r\n```c++\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) size_t test1(const char *ch, size_t size) {\r\n\treturn strnlen(ch, size);\r\n}\r\n\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) size_t test2(const char *ch, size_t size) {\r\n\treturn _strlen_clipped(ch, size);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nThis resulted in:\r\n- `248ms` (new code)\r\n- `2916ms` (current master)\r\n\r\nThe only beneficiary by this point is GDExtension code, because other `_strlen_clipped` callers have been eliminated already.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/event